must_fix.fix:
Pick one rule and write it down. Recommended: the note may frame, never assert. It must not state any event, consequence or causal claim in ARCHV's own voice. It may point to what to watch, or put a question as a statement of what is unknown, and nothing else. Add hard fails for:
- a note that omits attribution ("ESPN reports", "according to ESPN") when the headline or summary contains "Sources", "reportedly", "expected", "in talks", "could" or "set to";
- any past-tense completion verb (signed, traded, fired, completed, won) that is absent from the item;
- a negation that does not appear in the item.
Keep the name check as a hard fail, not a warning. Keep a human-readable log of rejected notes so drift shows up in week one.

